# HeroUI v3 Web Rules - MCP Integration

This rule set helps AI agents work with HeroUI v3 web components using the @heroui/mcp tools for accurate, up-to-date documentation and implementation guidance.

**Important Context**: https://v3.heroui.com/llms.txt - Reference this for additional HeroUI v3 context.

## Core Architecture

### HeroUI v3 is built on:
1. **Tailwind CSS v4** (v3 is NOT supported)
2. **React Aria Components** - For accessibility and behavior (@heroui/react)
3. **Framework-agnostic styles** - BEM classes via @heroui/styles

## MCP Tools Overview

The HeroUI MCP server provides these tools. Always use them instead of guessing component APIs:

### Essential Tools for HeroUI Development

1. **list_components** - Get all available components

   ```javascript
   // Always check available components first, use the version from package.json (if not latest)
   { library: "heroui", version?: "latest" }
   ```

2. **get_component_info** - Get complete component details including anatomy (if applicable)

   ```javascript
   // Use this before implementing any component
   { library: "heroui", component: "Button" }
   // Returns: description, anatomy, props, examples
   ```

3. **get_component_props** - Get detailed prop types

   ```javascript
   // Use when you need TypeScript types or prop validation
   { library: "heroui", component: "Card" }
   ```

4. **get_component_examples** - Get usage patterns

   ```javascript
   // Use for implementation examples
   { library: "heroui", component: "Button" }
   ```

5. **get_theme_info** - Get CSS variables and theme tokens

   ```javascript
   // Essential for customization
   { theme: "default", mode: "both", category: "all" }
   ```

6. **get_design_guide** - Get design documentation
   ```javascript
   // For theming and customization guidance
   {
     guide: "color-customization" | "custom-themes" | "dark-mode";
   }
   ```

## Component Implementation Rules

### 1. Always Verify Component API

Before implementing any HeroUI component:

- Use `get_component_info` to get the current API
- Never assume prop names or component structure
- Check for compound components (e.g., Card.Header, Card.Content)

### 2. Component Anatomy Pattern

HeroUI v3 uses compound components. Always check anatomy using the `get_component_info` tool:

```jsx
// CORRECT - Use compound components
<Card>
  <Card.Header>
    <Card.Title>Title</Card.Title>
  </Card.Header>
  <Card.Content>Content</Card.Content>
  <Card.Footer>Footer</Card.Footer>
</Card>

// WRONG - Don't use flat props
<Card title="Title" content="Content" />
```

### 3. Import Patterns

```jsx
// React Components (with full accessibility)
import {Button, Card, Avatar} from "@heroui/react";

// Framework-agnostic styles (CSS only, no JavaScript behavior)
import "@heroui/styles/dist/heroui.min.css";
// Or via CDN:
// <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@heroui/styles@3.0.0-alpha.31/dist/heroui.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
```

### 4. Framework-Agnostic Usage (HTML + CSS)

HeroUI v3 provides BEM classes via @heroui/styles for use without React:

```html
<!-- CDN link -->
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@heroui/styles@3.0.0-alpha.31/dist/heroui.min.css" rel="stylesheet" crossorigin="anonymous" />

<!-- BEM class pattern: component component--variant component--size -->
<div class="space-x-2 p-4">
  <button class="button button--primary button--md">Primary</button>
  <button class="button button--secondary button--md">Secondary</button>
  <button class="button button--tertiary button--md">Tertiary</button>
  <button class="button button--danger button--md">Danger</button>
  <button class="button button--ghost button--md">Ghost</button>
</div>

<!-- Note: This provides styling only. No JavaScript behavior, accessibility features,
     or interactive logic (open/close, focus management, etc.) -->
```

## Styling and Theming Rules

### 1. CSS Variables System

HeroUI uses CSS custom properties. Always use `get_theme_info` to get accurate variables:

```css
/* Theme variables follow this pattern */
--{category}-{semantic}-{variant}

/* Examples */
--color-accent          /* Semantic color */
--spacing-4            /* Spacing token */
--radius-medium        /* Border radius */
--ease-in-out-cubic    /* Animation timing */
```

### 2. Color System

HeroUI v3 uses OKLCH color space for better perceptual uniformity:

```css
/* OKLCH format: oklch(lightness chroma hue) */
--color-accent: oklch(0.7 0.25 260); /* L: 0-1, C: 0-0.4, H: 0-360 */
```

### 3. Theme Structure

```javascript
// Theme has three layers - always query with get_theme_info
{
  base: [],      // Primitives: --white, --black, spacing
  semantic: [],  // Purpose-driven: --accent, --success
  calculated: [] // Dynamic: hover states, computed values
}
```

### 4. Dark Mode

```jsx
// HeroUI handles dark mode via CSS classes
<html className="dark">  // or [data-theme="dark"]

// Component automatically adapts
<Button>Auto-adapts to dark mode</Button>
```

## Customization Patterns

### 1. Custom Theme Creation

Always use `get_design_guide` with guide="custom-themes" first, then:

```jsx
// 1. Define CSS variables
const customTheme = {
  light: {
    "--color-accent": "oklch(0.65 0.3 250)",
    "--color-success": "oklch(0.7 0.25 140)",
  },
  dark: {
    "--color-accent": "oklch(0.75 0.25 250)",
    "--color-success": "oklch(0.65 0.2 140)",
  },
};

// 2. Apply via CSS-in-JS or CSS files
// 3. Use data-theme attribute for switching
```

### 2. Component Styling

```jsx
// Use className for Tailwind classes
<Button className="px-8 py-4">Large Button</Button>

// Use style prop for CSS variables
<Card style={{padding: '2rem'}}>
  Custom padding
</Card>

// Component-specific classes
<Button className="heroui-button-custom">
  Custom styles
</Button>
```

### 3. Extending Components

```jsx
// Wrap HeroUI components for consistent styling
const CustomButton = ({variant = "accent", ...props}) => {
  // Always check props with get_component_props first
  return <Button className={`custom-${variant}`} {...props} />;
};
```

## Animation System

### 1. Built-in Animations

Use `get_theme_info` with category="animations" to get:

- Timing functions: --ease-in-quad, --ease-out-cubic
- Presets: --animate-spin-fast, --animate-skeleton

### 2. Custom Animations

```css
/* Use HeroUI timing functions */
.custom-animation {
  transition: all 0.3s var(--ease-out-cubic);
}

/* Reference animation presets */
.loading {
  animation: var(--animate-skeleton);
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Tool Usage Priority

1. **ALWAYS** use MCP tools before implementing
2. **NEVER** guess component APIs or prop names
3. **CHECK** version compatibility with `check_version`

### 2. Implementation Workflow

```javascript
// 1. Check component exists
list_components({library: "heroui"});

// 2. Get full documentation
get_component_info({library: "heroui", component: "Card"});

// 3. Get examples for patterns
get_component_examples({library: "heroui", component: "Card"});

// 4. Get theme variables if customizing
get_theme_info({mode: "both", category: "colors"});

// 5. Implement with accurate API
```

### 3. Common Patterns

#### Form Controls

```jsx
// TextField uses compound pattern
<TextField>
  <TextField.Label>Email</TextField.Label>
  <TextField.Input type="email" />
  <TextField.Error>Invalid email</TextField.Error>
</TextField>
```

#### Layout Components

```jsx
// Card with full anatomy
<Card>
  <Card.Image src="/image.jpg" alt="Description" />
  <Card.Header>
    <Card.Title>Title</Card.Title>
    <Card.Description>Description</Card.Description>
  </Card.Header>
  <Card.Content>Main content</Card.Content>
  <Card.Footer>
    <Button>Action</Button>
  </Card.Footer>
</Card>
```

#### Interactive Components

```jsx
// Tabs with compound structure
<Tabs defaultValue="tab1">
  <Tabs.List>
    <Tabs.Tab value="tab1">Tab 1</Tabs.Tab>
    <Tabs.Tab value="tab2">Tab 2</Tabs.Tab>
  </Tabs.List>
  <Tabs.Panel value="tab1">Content 1</Tabs.Panel>
  <Tabs.Panel value="tab2">Content 2</Tabs.Panel>
</Tabs>
```

## Debugging Tips

### 1. Component Not Working

1. Use `get_component_info` to verify correct API
2. Check import path is correct
3. Verify compound component structure

### 2. Styling Issues

1. Use `get_theme_info` to get correct CSS variables
2. Check dark mode class application
3. Verify OKLCH color values are valid

### 3. Props Not Recognized

1. Use `get_component_props` for accurate prop types
2. Check for compound component props
3. Verify version compatibility

