## Integration with Tailwind CSS v4

```javascript
// tailwind.config.js - MUST use Tailwind v4
import heroui from "@heroui/theme";

export default {
  content: [
    "./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}",
    "./node_modules/@heroui/theme/dist/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}",
  ],
  darkMode: "class",
  plugins: [heroui()],
};
```

**IMPORTANT**: HeroUI v3 requires Tailwind CSS v4. Tailwind v3 is NOT supported.

## React Aria Components Foundation

@heroui/react is built on React Aria Components, providing:
- Full keyboard navigation
- Screen reader support
- Focus management
- ARIA attributes
- Touch/mobile interactions

```jsx
// HeroUI components include all React Aria behaviors
<Button onPress={handlePress}>
  Fully accessible button with React Aria
</Button>

// Compared to BEM classes (styling only)
<button class="button button--primary">
  Visual styling only, no built-in a11y
</button>
```

## Key Differences from Other UI Libraries

1. **Tailwind v4 Required**: Not compatible with Tailwind v3
2. **React Aria Based**: Full accessibility out of the box with @heroui/react
3. **Framework Agnostic Styles**: BEM classes available via @heroui/styles
4. **Compound Components**: Not single components with many props
5. **OKLCH Colors**: Not hex or RGB
6. **CSS Variables**: Not CSS-in-JS by default
7. **Anatomy-based**: Each part is styleable separately
8. **Theme Layers**: Base, semantic, and calculated variables

## Usage Modes Summary

### 1. React with Full Accessibility (@heroui/react)
- Built on React Aria Components
- Full keyboard navigation, screen readers, ARIA
- Interactive behaviors included
- Requires Tailwind CSS v4

### 2. Framework-Agnostic Styles (@heroui/styles)
- BEM class patterns
- Visual styling only
- No JavaScript behaviors
- No accessibility features
- Can be used with any framework or vanilla HTML

